    {
      "name": "citybeat-directory-ingest",
      "pausedReason": "Overpass refuses connections from this service's GCP egress: the recorded failures are `fetch failed` for all 7 categories and a single-category call returns 500 in 3.9s, which is two instant connection failures plus the backoff, not the 2x45s a timeout would take. The IPv6 theory was tested and refuted (api.resend.com, api.anthropic.com, kvia.com and firestore.googleapis.com all carry AAAA and all work from the same container). No env var fixes a refusal at the far end, and the only IPv4-only mirrors are a dead Japanese host and a Russian one. Paused 2026-10-28 after failing every night since 2026-10-15. The route is unchanged and OVERPASS_URL is still the no-deploy escape hatch, so re-enabling is: unpause, restore state ENABLED here, and restore the cron:directory-ingest entry in CRON_EXPECTATIONS. Directory growth now comes from the Socrata feeds, which reach us fine.",
      "schedule": "0 2 * * *",
      "timeZone": "America/Chihuahua",
      "uri": "https://citybeat-web-aa3zf3nfza-uc.a.run.app/api/cron/directory-ingest",
